<!DOCTYPE html>
<html dir="{{ direction }}" lang="{{ lang }}"{% if mc_preset %} data-mc-preset="{{ mc_preset }}"{% endif %}>
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<base href="{{ base }}" />
{% if description %}
<meta name="description" content="{{ description }}" />
{% endif %}
{% if keywords %}
<meta name="keywords" content="{{ keywords }}" />
{% endif %}
{% if mc_robots_content %}
<meta name="robots" content="{{ mc_robots_content }}" />
{% endif %}
{#
    MintCart's own compiled assets/dist/{css,js} bundle: this wrapper
    deliberately keeps the exact same legacy asset stack
    `default/template/common/header.twig` loads below (Bootstrap 3,
    jQuery, Font Awesome, common.js) rather than replacing it - swapping
    it out safely still needs the full call-site audit of every page/
    widget that depends on jQuery/common.js/Bootstrap-3 markup (cart AJAX,
    form validation, account pages, checkout) per CLAUDE.md §10/§84, not
    attempted here. See docs/developer/components/header.md "Known gap:
    MintCart's own asset bundle is not enqueued yet" for that remaining
    piece.

    What *is* enqueued now (`ControllerCommonHeader::index()`, added via
    the `styles`/`scripts` loops right below, gated behind the same
    isMintAware() check `mc_header` uses - see that controller for the
    full writeup): `assets/dist/css/components.min.css` +
    `assets/dist/js/catalog.min.js`. Not `index.min.css` - that one was
    tried directly on 2026-08-24 (live install check) and confirmed
    broken: it bundles full Bootstrap 5 CSS
    (`@import 'bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.css'` in
    assets/src/css/index.css), and loading that alongside the Bootstrap 3
    stack below redefines `.container`/`.row`/`.btn`/`.modal`/etc. out
    from under it - not theoretical, it visibly shrank body text, broke
    the `.navbar-nav`/dropdown menus, and made the search widget overlap
    the cart widget on a real page. `components.min.css`
    (docs/developer/admin/asset-enqueue.md) is the same bundle with only
    that Bootstrap 5 import removed - every remaining `mc-*`/`--mc-*`
    selector was grepped and confirmed to never touch a bare element or a
    Bootstrap class name, so it coexists with the Bootstrap 3 stack below
    without reverting or reworking any of it. `catalog.min.js` is plain ES
    modules with no jQuery coupling, so it does not collide with
    common.js/jQuery/Bootstrap 3's own bootstrap.min.js either.
#}
<script src="catalog/view/javascript/jquery/jquery-3.7.1.min.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
<link href="catalog/view/javascript/bootstrap/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet" media="screen" />
<script src="catalog/view/javascript/bootstrap/js/bootstrap.min.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
<link href="catalog/view/javascript/font-awesome/css/font-awesome.min.css" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" />
<link href="//fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Open+Sans:400,400i,300,700" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" />
<link href="catalog/view/theme/default/stylesheet/stylesheet.css" rel="stylesheet">
{% for style in styles %}
<link href="{{ style.href }}" type="text/css" rel="{{ style.rel }}" media="{{ style.media }}" />
{% endfor %}
{% for script in scripts %}
<script src="{{ script }}" type="text/javascript"></script>
{% endfor %}
<script src="catalog/view/javascript/common.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
{% for link in links %}
<link href="{{ link.href }}" rel="{{ link.rel }}" />
{% endfor %}
{% for analytic in analytics %}
{{ analytic }}
{% endfor %}
{% if mc_schema_organization %}
<script type="application/ld+json">{{ mc_schema_organization|raw }}</script>
{% endif %}
</head>
<body>
{{ mc_header }}
